-- title:
--   Twisted place count on the Drinfeld curve at elliptic classes
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $k$ an algebraically closed field equipped with an $\mathbb{F}_{q^2} =$ `GaloisField q 2`-algebra structure, such that the coordinate ring `CoordRing q k`, namely the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`, is a domain, and such that its fraction field $F =$ `drinfeldFunctionField q k` is a curve over $k$ in the sense of [`AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver`](def/AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver.html#L15): every nonzero element of $F$ has a degree-zero principal divisor, every place of $F$ over $k$ has residue field finite over $k$, and $\Omega_{F/k}$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$. Let $\varphi : F \to F$ be a $k$-algebra endomorphism whose underlying ring map is integral and which satisfies $\varphi(x) = x^{q^2}$ and $\varphi(y) = y^{q^2}$ on the images of the coordinates `x q k`, `y q k` in $F$. Let $\alpha \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ be a unit whose underlying element does not lie in the image of $\mathbb{Z}/q \to \mathbb{F}_{q^2}$, let $\zeta \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$, and suppose the pair $(\mathrm{torus}\,\alpha, \zeta)$ — where $\mathrm{torus}\,\alpha \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ is the matrix of multiplication by $\alpha$ on $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ in the basis `quadBasis q` — lies in `hSubgroup q`, the kernel of the character sending $(g,\zeta)$ to $\det(g)\cdot\zeta^{q+1}$ in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$. Consider the set of places $w$ of $F$ over $k$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $k$, proper, and principal ideal rings) such that the pullback `Place.restrictAlong φ hφi w`, the comap of $w$ along $\varphi$, equals the translate of $w$ by the $k$-automorphism of $F$ induced by $(\mathrm{torus}\,\alpha,\zeta)$ through `hFunctionFieldAction q k`. The theorem asserts two implications: if $-\zeta^{-1} = \alpha$ or $-\zeta^{-1} = \alpha^{q}$ then this set has cardinality $q+1$, and otherwise it has cardinality $(q+1)^2$.
--
--   This is the Deligne–Lusztig style point count for the $h$-twisted Frobenius on the Drinfeld curve $xy^q - x^qy = 1$ at the classes $h = (\mathrm{torus}\,\alpha,\zeta)$ coming from the non-split (elliptic) torus of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_q)$; the two values $q+1$ and $(q+1)^2$ encode the Lefschetz numbers on which the cuspidality of the associated representations rests. It is used in the proof that the twisted intertwining map vanishes for cuspidal types over an algebraically closed field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_natCard_place_restrictAlong_eq_smul_of_torus.lean

